From 25d58bd7f6782ee0d4185055741898b25cb5a16c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jmgasper <jmgasper@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:12:52 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] nvrm: run on Pascal, and map sub-page allocations
 correctly

A mapping the driver returns covers whole pages, because RM rounds the
mapping context's ranges down to a page boundary.  A channel's USERD is
512 bytes and several channels share one page, so every channel after
the first was writing its GPPut into the first channel's USERD: the
wrong channel was kicked, the submitting channel never ran, and nothing
it submitted ever completed.  pLinearAddress carries the offset inside
the page, so add it back, as the Linux driver's callers do.

The rest makes NVK work on a pre-Volta GPU: channels have no doorbell
and no work submit token, USERD comes from RM's FIFO mapping instead of
our own buffer, completion uses the GF100 semaphore methods, engine
objects are only allocated for the classes the GPU has, and block
linear allocations accept PTE kind 0xfe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
